// Deer Valley maps as a RUSSL-Zarr multiscale Penteract field, generated by the living map law.
// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
//
// Field: shape (1, 1, C, H, W) with c6 = map channel, c7 = y, c8 = x (RUSSL-OME-ZARR/2.0.0 axis order
// (t, z, c, y, x) = (n4 .. n8)). Levels 0..7 cover the same 512 m x 512 m torus at 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4, 8,
// 16 and 32 m per sample. Chunks are 128 x 128 samples (the Zarr chunk grid), generated on demand.
//
// The living map law (deer.valley.living/1) turns the simulation's 4 m terrain into a 1 m relief that keeps
// changing with the valley. It uses integer arithmetic only (IEEE + - x / on integers below 2^53, floor and
// comparisons), so one seed and one history give the same bytes and SHA-256 roots on every machine.
//
//   genesis    the simulation terrain upsampled 4x by exact Catmull-Rom; relief above the lake x 3/2;
//              domain-warped detail; bedrock with strata where the ground is rocky; then five rain passes:
//     route    a priority flood from the lake: every sample drains to a lower neighbour. Each closed
//              depression is a cycle of drain claims that cannot all hold (E17); filling resolves it, and the
//              lowest sample and the spill height are kept as its witness.
//     value    the drainage area A and its E14 discounted path value V (gamma = 7/8): stream power and wetness
//     incise   stream power A^1/2 S erodes; a transport capacity proportional to A S deposits the excess;
//              what reaches the lake settles as deltas under the water
//     settle   talus relaxation to an exact fixed point (E8), certified by one quiet sweep. Every update reads
//              only a sample's neighbours (E11), and no pass creates or destroys mass: the sum of all heights
//              is exactly unchanged (E18).
//   materials  rock is the AND of thresholds on slope, erosion and bedrock (E20); moisture comes from V and the
//              shore; scree, gravel and stream beds from where the passes moved their mass
//   living     each epoch the herd's trail field compacts the soil along its paths, and unused paths recover
//              geometrically (E3); mid-spring rain, and every rain you bring, runs another pass where it falls.
//              The store's version and roots change with each generation, so each generation has its own map.
// Levels: 2 is the 1 m relief; 0-1 refine/2 (Catmull-Rom plus roughness by material); 3-7 decimate2. The
// channel "terrain" keeps the simulation's own terrain, exact at level 4 (the map R file seals both).
